WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.760
650 drones aimed at Moscow kill one man, Russian officials say. This is Omni View Europe, episode 14. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. France 24 reports Ukraine sent that wave overnight, and Russian authorities called it one of the biggest hits on the capital in two years. The state agency TAS ranks its second largest against Moscow and the region around it in that stretch. Mayor Sergei Sobianin says Russian defenses brought down most of the drones,

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.980
and 105 of them fell close to the city itself.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.620
Governor Andre Voribyova says the dead man was 20

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.360
in a village on the outskirts,

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.480
and that several houses were damaged.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:43.320
Rio Novosti puts the wounded at six.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:47.720
France 24 says both armies have increased long range hits on homes,

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:50.620
factories, energy sites, transport,

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:52.580
ports, and black sea ships.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:55.240
And Moscow says it will hit more infrastructure,

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.500
including in Kiev, as winter comes.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:02.380
across the region, Brussels has stopped a factory subsidy in southern Poland.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:07.840
The European Commission says Poland may not hand MAN trucks about 26 million Euros,

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:13.540
116 million Lodi, to add capacity at Neapolomice in Malapolskie.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.840
Investigators opened the file in July 2025.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:21.020
Early on, the Commission thought the plant would bring work to a poor region,

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:23.620
then doubted it fitted the regional aid guidelines.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:31.580
The full inquiry found Poland never proved the cash made M-A-N pickpulland, and nothing showed the firm would have built somewhere else without it.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:39.440
Brussels also says Warsaw never showed the sum was the smallest that would do the job, so the grant had no real pull and was out of proportion.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:48.500
In Britain, ministers said on the 6th of October, they will take all 44 ideas from the National Commission into the regulation of AI in healthcare,

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:52.420
published on the 10th of September and apply them across the UK.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.660
The Commission wants a lighter system that follows a device

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:58.700
for its whole working life, not a single check at the door.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.660
The Medicines Regulator has opened phase 3 of AI airlock,

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:05.780
so developers, regulators, and hospitals can test

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:08.360
how those tools are watched after they go into use.

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.500
Applicants get a webinar on the 22nd of October.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.880
Draft guidance on how changing AI devices are handled

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:20.500
is promised by December 2026, and a consultation on how to class them starts next year.

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:27.300
Also today, Norwegian jets had tagged 107 Russian military aircraft by the 29th of September,

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:31.840
against 53 in all of last year, after 77 scrambles,

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:36.300
and the Air Force told Norwegian broadcasters NATO airspace was not crossed.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:41.060
In Bosnia, Sunday's general election left the Party of Democratic Action,

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:46.100
The Croatian Democratic Union and the Alliance of Independent Social Democrats each still

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:50.840
strongest in their own ethnic camp on a record low turnout, Balkan Insight Reports.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:56.680
In Barcelona, thousands marched on Monday for cheaper homes, then some through objects

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:01.800
in lit rubbish bins, police detained several people, and Spain's government has set a snap

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.800
election for the 29th of November, Euro news reports.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:11.260
In Ireland, hotel contracts cover more than 4,000 Ukrainians and next month, and payments

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:14.340
to private hosts end in March, the Irish Times reports.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:19.440
The case on both sides today is whether new European Union members should face limits

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.700
before they get a full seat.

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:26.220
Keeve-Post says the European Commission is due to put proposals out on Tuesday after months

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.820
of delay while capitals argued.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:32.900
Diplomats expect rules so newcomers cannot jam decisions or take too large a share

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:37.560
of subsidies, including no veto in key fields and a cap on farm payments.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:42.680
In large-met commissioner Marta Koss said in August, we must make sure we do not let

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:47.100
intrusion horses, and call those checks a must-have, not a nice-to-have.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:52.220
The worry in that reporting is that new members, above all Ukraine, could strain the budget

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:56.760
and clog decisions, with Hungary's blocks under Victor Orbán held up as the warning.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:02.080
Chancellor Friedrich Mards earlier this year offered associate membership, a seat in the

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:06.180
room and no vote. Ukraine and a raft of EU countries gave that short

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:10.420
drift, reading it as a permanent halfway house, and there is also pushback

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:13.860
against rushing entry. Both camps start from the same list.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:18.880
Russia's 2022 invasion restarted the enlargement drive. Ukraine and

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:23.980
Moldova are among four frontrunners. Montenegro wants to be member 28 next year.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:30.780
Albania is close behind. Brussels says enlargement matters to the

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:32.640
The Step Keeve Post says comes today.

